WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:05.410
We suspected it for the last two days and
Republican Senate majority leader Mitch McConnell

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:11.420
is now admitting that Republicans do not yet
have the votes to successfully block impeachment

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:16.500
witnesses in the Senate trial of Donald Trump.
Now, yet is a key word. Remember that in the

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.939
past we've seen reports that Mitch McConnell
didn't have the votes to confirm Brett Kavanaugh

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:25.439
to the Supreme court. Brett, Kevin, eyes now
on the Supreme court. So anytime we hear from

00:00:25.439 --> 00:00:30.140
Mitch McConnell that he doesn't yet have the
votes, we have to understand that that may

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.739
be a game that he's playing.

00:00:31.739 --> 00:00:36.290
The latest word is that witness related votes
are going to happen on Friday in the Senate.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:39.940
McConnell says, hopefully by then they will
have the votes. Remember that witnesses are

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:44.841
dependent on a a C, a simple majority in the
Senate. So you don't need two thirds. You

00:00:44.841 --> 00:00:51.240
need just 51 senators to say we want witnesses.
That would be the 45 Democrats, two independent

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:56.900
senators, Angus King and Bernie Sanders and
for Republicans, we suspect that Mitt Romney

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.630
and Susan Collins might be two of those four
Republicans. New reports suggest there could

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:06.830
be many more Republicans planning to vote
for witnesses, but until they do it, we don't

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:12.650
know. And as I said yesterday, Republicans
are remarkably unreliable at doing the right

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:17.640
thing. So let's not speculate any further.
Let's focus on the facts and the reality of

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:23.860
a trial and witnesses. Trials should have
witnesses. 75% of the country wants witnesses

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:29.200
per a new Quinnipiac poll, which we are linking
to, Republicans have complained that they

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:35.740
have not seen any firsthand testimony of what
Donald Trump did and wanted to have done.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.340
Donald Trump's former national security advisor,
John Bolton, is willing to testify and is

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:45.060
likely to say what he says in his upcoming
book, which is Trump told him to withhold

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:51.251
aid to Ukraine until Ukraine smears Joe Biden
publicly. That's a firsthand witness. He's

00:01:51.251 --> 00:01:55.870
willing to testify. Republicans claim they
want firsthand witnesses, but they are trying

00:01:55.870 --> 00:02:01.980
to block John Bolton from testifying. Republicans
started signaling their talking points to

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.630
argue against witnesses a few days ago. They
are three main talking points. Republicans

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:12.770
are using, number one, they've started saying,
well, after we do 64 hours of stuff, 24 hours

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:18.480
of house managers, 24 hours of Trump's lawyers,
16 hours of Senator questions, then we can

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.349
decide if we really need to hear more. And
the implication is it's all kind of the same,

00:02:23.349 --> 00:02:27.360
right? 24 hours of Adam Schiff is the same
as hearing from John Bolton. It's just more

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:32.960
hours. Of course, this is part of the gaslighting
because John Bolton can actually tell us what

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.940
Donald Trump did.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:40.370
This is incorrect. It's gaslighting, but they're
going to try it. Secondly, they are trying

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:46.020
a strategy of if Democrats get witnesses,
we get witnesses too because this can't just

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:52.120
be one sided. Now the determination about
who testifies shouldn't be about uh, the,

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:55.900
the party affiliation or which side wants
the witness. The question should be, are they

00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:01.430
material witnesses? Republicans have signaled
that if John Bolton testifies, they might

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:07.239
want Joe Biden to testify. They might want
Hunter Biden to testify. This is gaslighting.

00:03:07.239 --> 00:03:11.870
The Biden's have nothing to do with determining
the guilt or innocence of Donald Trump. Republicans

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:16.620
want to make it about Joe Biden, but it's
not. Bolton is a firsthand witness to what

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:21.950
Donald Trump did. Trump is on trial, not Joe
Biden, so that's the second gaslighting strategy.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:27.330
They will try. Number three, Republicans will
say, Democrats could have called these witnesses

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:30.129
when they had hearings in the house. They
don't get to do it now.

00:03:30.129 --> 00:03:35.030
Now, of course, that's illegally and historically
invalid. You don't have to call every in the

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:38.650
house the same that you don't have to call
every witness in a grand jury that you eventually

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:44.349
call in the trial. The Senate is a valid place
to call witnesses. They had the option of

00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:48.720
subpoenaing John Bolton in the house. It could
have taken a year or longer for that subpoena

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.880
to work its way through the judiciary and
nothing would have happened. So that is a

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:59.290
misdirection. Those are the three most common
arguments that we're hearing from Republicans

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:04.290
against hearing from witnesses. Last thought,
let me go back to the beginning. Mitch McConnell

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:08.860
says they don't yet have the votes to block
witnesses. He has said this before and gotten

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:14.620
the votes. This could be a ploy to make it
look like they're really deliberating. Republicans

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:19.049
are really taking it seriously and really
thinking through do they want to have witnesses

00:04:19.049 --> 00:04:20.739
and if so, which one?

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:25.580
And then when they say no on Friday, if they
don't get the votes, they can say it wasn't

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:29.840
a foregone conclusion. We took all week to
deliberate. We thought about it really hard.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.220
We didn't think we had the votes, and in the
end we did. So I will believe that four Republicans

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:39.680
are going to vote for witnesses. When for
Republicans, vote for witnesses in the Senate,

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:44.979
which may happen on Friday. Tell me what you
think will happen. Will John Bolton ultimately

